7afeb211071894ee8b071292695d463f280be"} {"question" "q-91211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-5{C}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-3{C}_{4}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071806/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee57a6ecf8cbd0b21df5f6a02c77afeb211071894ee8b071292695d463f280be"} {"question" "q-91212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 9 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -16 & 8 & -16 & -20 \\\\ -12 & 9 & -17 & -24 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\n- ${C}_{1}:=…$\n- ${C}_{3}:=…$\n- ${C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-3{C}_{2}$\n\neach of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071806/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee57a6ecf8cbd0b21df5f6a02c77afeb211071894ee8b071292695d463f280be"} {"question" "q-91212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 9 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -16 & 8 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -12 & 9 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -16 & 8 & -16 & 4 \\\\ -12 & 9 & -17 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -16 & 8 & -16 & -20 \\\\ -12 & 9 & -17 & -24 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071806/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee57a6ecf8cbd0b21df5f6a02c77afeb211071894ee8b071292695d463f280be"} {"question" "q-91212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5246ce69646f54fde2612ae5c1932087252ff7d55f96a6e822db8639d944be9b"} {"question" "q-91212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071806/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee57a6ecf8cbd0b21df5f6a02c77afeb211071894ee8b071292695d463f280be"} {"question" "q-91212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{2}$"] ["text" "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{2}$"] ["text" "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}$"] ["text" "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-3{C}_{2}$"] ["text" "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071806/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee57a6ecf8cbd0b21df5f6a02c77afeb211071894ee8b071292695d463f280be"} {"question" "q-91212" "field" "selection" "attribute"